cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SweepLSD in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "SweepLSD"
abstract: >-
  A line segment detector that reads the image exactly once, top to bottom.
  Every stage — including connected-component labelling and the final line
  test — processes the image as a row stream, so intermediate memory is
  O(width) rather than O(pixels) and the per-pixel core is integer-only.
  Ships as a dependency-free C++17 library plus synthesizable HLS C++ and
  Verilog RTL that run live on an FPGA at 1080p30 with no frame buffer.
type: software
